// features: func-call, locals, print, std-math, std-str, string-literal
// Bare `ns.func` spellings of *pure-ZZ* stdlib helpers — no native twin,
// so the body only exists when the module joins the compiled closure.
// Imports used to be the only thing that put it there: `zz check` passed
// via the canonical fallback, then the VM failed at run time with
// `undefined method `repeat``, while the HIR backend merged every
// reachable stdlib program and silently succeeded (#503).
//
// The reference scan in the loader now records those namespaces, so all
// engines agree. Bare *natives* (`str.length`) stay legal everywhere and
// must not drag a module in.
func main() {
    println(str.repeat("ab", 2))
    println(str.reverse("abc"))
    println(str.is_empty(""))
    println(math.min(1, 2))
    println(math.sum([1, 2, 3]))
    println(str.length("abc"))
    println("bare_purezz_call_ok")
}
